    <!-- About -->
    <string name="about_intro">AstroScout helps you find the best spot for astrophotography by combining light pollution, astronomical weather and nearby parking.</string>
    <string name="about_simulated">Warning: no DarkSkySites API key is configured. Light pollution values come from a simplified SIMULATION and must not be used to plan real sessions.</string>
    <string name="about_score_formula" formatted="false">Astro Score = 100 × Σ(weight × sub-score) / Σ(weights). Light pollution: linear on SQM from 17.5 to 22.0 mag/arcsec². Clouds: 1 − mean cover during astronomical darkness (Open-Meteo, else 7Timer!; 0 if precipitation). Seeing and transparency: (8 − 7Timer! index) / 7. Moon: f + (1 − f)·(1 − k), f = moon-free share of the dark hours, k = illuminated fraction (×0.6 with only nautical twilight). Altitude: 0 m → 0, 2000 m → 1. With cover ≥ 80% or precipitation the score is capped at 20. Sun and Moon are computed on the phone (Meeus algorithms).</string>
